# Never commit `.codegen`

The `.codegen/` directory holds local `zero-codegen` tooling. It must **never** be staged, committed, or pushed to GitHub (or any remote).

- Do not `git add .codegen` or force-add ignored paths under `.codegen/`.
- If asked to commit “everything”, exclude `.codegen/`.
- On a fresh clone, obtain `.codegen` from `zero-apps-codegen-scaffold` (see README), then run `pnpm codegen:paths`.
